The files `bridge.js` and `select.js` in this directory are adapted from
Corex v0.2.2 (https://github.com/corex-ui/corex, git tag v0.2.2), which is
also MIT-licensed. Specifically:

- `bridge.js` derives from Corex `assets/lib/zag-live-hook.ts`,
  `assets/lib/core.ts`, and the select subset of `assets/lib/util.ts`,
  `assets/lib/respond-to.ts`, `assets/lib/read-props.ts`,
  `assets/lib/dom-events.ts`, `assets/lib/hook-handlers.ts`,
  `assets/lib/controlled-attr-snapshot.ts`, and
  `assets/lib/list-collection.ts`.
- `select.js` derives from Corex `assets/components/select.ts` and
  `assets/hooks/select.ts`.

Adaptations: translated from TypeScript to plain JS, renamed the
`corex:*` event namespace to `lantern:*`, dropped groups / redirect /
form-array protocol / per-instance positioning (lantern options are flat
`{value, label}` pairs), kept lantern's toggle-label and `max` contracts.
Per the task contract the Corex package itself is NOT a dependency —
only the shared `@zag-js/*` engine it (and now lantern) builds on.

